    "measurementTechnique": [
      "Geomorphic mapping was done by hand in QGIS 3.4 on Landsat ~30-m and Worldview 2-m imagery. Mapping includes geomorphic landforms visible on the floodplain, the relative age of groups of landforms based on cross-cutting relationships, and inferred prior paths of the river based on the location of oxbow lakes. All datasets are projected in WGS84.",
      "Permafrost occurrence was measured through probing, coring or digging sampling pits, and direct observation of ground ice in riverbanks. Permafrost probing is capable of detecting ice-cemented sediment that resists penetration, which is characteristic of most permafrost in the floodplain based on observations of cores and pits. The depth of thaw was measured in the vertical direction on the floodplain surface and in the horizontal direction on steep, exposed faces of eroding riverbanks."
    ],
